---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Adiviath Technologies" description="Adiviath Technologies makes niche software for specific real-world needs.">
  <section class="page-hero about-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Adiviath</p>
    <h1>Useful beats universal.</h1>
    <p>We are a technology company that builds focused products for real, specific ways of working.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-grid">
    <h2>Why we exist</h2>
    <div>
      <p class="lead">Good software does not need to serve everyone. It needs to serve its users exceptionally well.</p>
      <p>
        Adiviath starts with a workflow people already depend on. We learn where it
        slows down, where information gets lost, and where generic tools stop fitting.
        Then we build the smallest complete product that makes that work better.
      </p>
      <p>Pharmulo, our platform for pharmaceutical wholesalers, is the first expression of that approach.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mark-story">
    <img src="/adiviath-mark.png" alt="Adiviath symbol" width="320" height="320" />
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Our mark</p>
      <h2>Software shaped around the need.</h2>
      <p>
        The orange core is the specific work that matters—a person’s task, a business
        workflow, or a problem generic software does not fit. The surrounding form is
        the product we shape around it, leaving room for the work to grow and change.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles">
    <article><span>01</span><h3>Start specific</h3><p>A clear user and a real workflow come before a feature list.</p></article>
    <article><span>02</span><h3>Fit the work</h3><p>The product adapts to the business instead of demanding a fresh system around it.</p></article>
    <article><span>03</span><h3>Stay useful</h3><p>We measure progress in daily friction removed, not software added.</p></article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
